SUMMARY:We the People First Friday: Heartland Marimba Festival
DESCRIPTION:Make the Ware Center for the Arts part of your Lancaster City F
 irst Friday route! Join us in November as Heartland Marimba presents a han
 ds-on\, behind-the-scenes look at the marimba\, and a new art exhibit open
 s in the Regitz Gallery. At 7 pm in the lobby\, join the members of Heartl
 and Marimba as they reveal all the insider goodies about their fascinating
  instrument. Listen\, touch\, and learn as you explore the science of its 
 acoustics\, trace its history from Africa to Central America to the classi
 cal music stage\, and hear the untold stories of the marimba’s Pennsylva
 nia roots—including tales of the “godfather” of classical marimba\, 
 Clair Musser\, who hailed from Manheim\, PA. From 5-8 in the Regitz Galler
 y\, explore a new gallery exhibit by Lancaster artist Shauna L. Yorty\, "O
 vershare: I Did This for Me." Through cardboard collages\, mixed media pie
 ces\, and bright\, bold works of art\, Yorty invites viewers to witness vu
 lnerability\, embrace their own stories\, and find connection to themselve
 s and to others through artistic expression. Free and open to all!\n\nPric
 e: Not supplied by this calendar\; check event details\n\nSchedule listed:
  Fri\, Nov 06\, 2026 07:00 PM EST – Fri\, Nov 06\, 2026 09:00 PM EST\n\n
